WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.940
Together...

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.060
Our passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.900
Aikatsu Stars! is about to start!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.490
Aikatsu Island is back again this year!

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.490
This summer, we've turned an entire tropical island into an idol theme park.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.500
At the moment, we're all in the thick of preparations.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.420
Could you check on that?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.580
Is this right?

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.040
Yes, that looks just fine.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:33.130
Headmaster, I seem to recall that you went over budget at last year's event.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.300
That is why this year will be a collaboration.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.140
As for the theme...

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.060
"Let's envelop everyone in the Aikatsu ring." {because they spend the entire episode going WA WA, and it's in the title like that, so it has to be snappy}

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.060
Right!

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.020
Ring!

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.570
Nobody's passing by.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.650
Yeah...

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.360
What now? Should we walk back?

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.530
I see one!

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.790
Excuse me!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.330
Hey!

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:01.910
Over here!

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.620
Yes, they stopped!

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.210
Hi, we're sorry to trouble you, but could we get a ride to the event grounds up ahead?

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.880
Of course, you got it!

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.860
But really, what happened?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.610
How'd you end up hitchhiking from there?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.070
We couldn't find the bus stop, and got completely lost after looking around.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.450
Oh?

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.490
I'm glad we drove by.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:09.160
You really saved us. We have a very important show to make.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.620
A show?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.670
We're holding an event on this island.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.750
You're welcome to come.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.130
Wow, this looks like fun!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.510
It does!

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.760
See for yourself!

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.260
Oh yeah, we never introduced ourselves.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.260
I'm Nijino Yume, from Four Star Academy.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.640
I'm her classmate, Sakuraba Rola.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.270
I'm Kasumi Mahiru.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.480
Nice to meet you.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.650
Huh...

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.280
Four Star Academy is an idol school.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.110
You're just like us!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.910
I'm Oozora Akari.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.660
Shinjou Hinaki.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.790
I'm Hikami Sumire.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.660
We're idols from Starlight Academy.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.920
What?!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.670
It's so nice to meet you! Let's be friends!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.840
I was just about to ask the same thing!

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.420
I'm really happy we met each other.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.340
Come on, let's drop the formalities. We're all Aikatsu buddies now.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.180
Yeah!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.390
Sure! And isn't this right in the spirit of this year's Aikatsu Island theme, Yume?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.230
Yep.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.690
Good point.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:14.940
Theme?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:20.610
It's this: Let's envelop everyone in the Aikatsu ring!

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.150
Like this?

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.360
Ring!

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.610
Ring!

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.490
Ring!

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:35.120
We all had the day off, so we decided to go check out some place we hadn't been before.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.380
We're slotted to be presenters for our senpai's performance.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.670
Sounds great.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.050
I'd love to see it!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:44.970
Me too.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.600
Then would you like to come with us?

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.810
We'll take you there.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.930
Come on.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.310
Sure, I'd like that.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:57.900
Yeah! Seeing shows of all kinds is an important part of Aikatsu.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.400
You said it!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.070
It's a plan!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.320
Subaru-kun messaged me.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.280
It says "mission complete". Great!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.280
Yume, what does he mean by mission?

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.160
I wanted to get something nice for Hime-senpai and the others.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.670
I had him subtly ask them what they wanted.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:22.260
Oh right, the guys are doing a dress rehearsal with them right now.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:31.140
The girls said that they'd be really happy with four-leaf clovers.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.430
Four-leaf clovers?

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.480
They do say they bring good fortune...

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.980
Can we find them in time for the show?

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.320
We'll help out, Yume-chan.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.820
If we all look together, we're sure to succeed.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.660
Right?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.490
Yeah!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.870
I know we can.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.160
Thank you, Akari-chan!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.090
But why four-leaf clovers, of all things?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.260
Cause here, take a look.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:10.550
Doesn't it look like four-leaf clovers are made up of four hearts put together as one? {well if you're gonna do that, then I'm gonna do this}

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.100
We're reuniting after all this time.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:22.020
Having four-leaf clovers to commemorate the occasion would be perfect.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.480
Yeah?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.650
Unfortunately...

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.610
I heard they're pretty hard to find.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.030
That's true.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.910
It'd be super lucky if we find one though!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.660
Four-leaf clover! Where are you?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.130
Clover! Come out, come out, wherever you are!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.300
Thanks again for helping us out.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.170
Hey, that's enough of that. 
I'm already having lots of fun!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.680
Look over there. The others seem to be having fun too.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.680
That's a relief.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.810
I hope your senpai will appreciate this.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.440
Me too! I love them all so much.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.770
Yeah, I get you!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.280
Really?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:12.110
Yeah, I have someone I admire just as much. She's a very special idol.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.870
Her name is Hoshimiya Ichigo-senpai.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.750
That person for me is Shiratori Hime-senpai.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.910
We're the same. {I do not get why Akari goes all "sou kamo"}{"it may be the case that the statement 'hime-senpai is that person to me' is true, but I am not sure because I do not know the details of your relationship with hime-senpai"}{naruhodo}

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.710
Yep!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.170
Anyway, we're not having much luck finding one.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.760
I'm sure they're here!

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:33.550
Maybe they're like the stars at daytime, and you're just unable to see them. {150 weeks later, and my first instinct was the exact same phrasing}

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.300
The stars at daytime?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:40.770
Yeah. Hoshimiya-senpai gave me these precious words. {I guess this takes place sometime before the epilogue}

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.650
Even during daytime, the stars don't disappear.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.820
Even if you can't see them, they're still twinkling.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.950
That's lovely!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:57.200
Four-leaf clovers are the same. Even if you can't find them, they're surely out there!{not sure if on purpose or}{upyo}

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.080
Yeah... even if we can't see them,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.420
they're shining somewhere out there. Somewhere!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.550
Ribbit?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.010
Geez, don't startle me like that!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.760
Found one!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.310
What's going on?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.730
You found one?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.730
Yeah!

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.020
Sweet! {fucking Hinaki. She uses this twice this episode, neither in the context of our usual "Heya". as such, I'm testing out this other surfer-esque lingo to fit the vivid kiss image}{tubular☆gnarly?}

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.190
You did it!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:28.230
We need enough for four people, so three to go.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.440
Okay, let's keep it up!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.150
Not so fast, Yume-chan.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.490
Akari-chan, what kind of sky is above us today? {at least it fits}

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:42.710
The forecast said there was going to be a short but strong downpour over the island.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:43.910
Really?

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:48.540
Yeah. The clouds are getting darker, and even the frogs are crying out.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.840
Believe it or not, Akari-chan is a weather idol!

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.970
Wow, that gets me going!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.930
It's raining... just like you said!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.260
Let's go find shelter!

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:00.720
Okay!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.140
Make a run for it!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.680
Wait up!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.810
We're suited up!

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.980
We're ready from head to toe!{I... guess}{tell Ako to stop saying perfect when Elza isn't around}

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.360
Head to toe...

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.650
It's from Yume-chan.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:19.530
She says they're looking for four-leaf clovers as a present to our senpai.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.660
Finding a clover or two is no match for my network.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.840
<i>Attention all M4 fan club members, this is a message from Ako.</i>

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.630
<i>I request your assistance in looking for four-leaf clovers!</i>

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.510
<i>Nyan!</i>

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.630
As a fellow M4 fan...

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.760
We'll always help a sister in need! {I see you consider the male members female too}

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.850
Perfectly done.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.140
That was amazing, Ako-chan!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:47.310
Rain always gets me down. {super wanna include melancholy}{go ahead}{I was hoping you'd do it}

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:52.110
There is no rain without end. Some things can only be discovered by stopping for a moment.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.030
Huh?

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:58.110
I tried to think of rain in a positive way. I do it often with fortune telling.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.450
Wow, you can tell fortunes?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.540
Yeah! Just a bit.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.750
Do you think you can try seeing where we can find a clover?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:06.790
Huh?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.920
Good idea. I'll give it a try.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.210
Well?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:21.180
It reads that a miracle will suddenly occur in an unexpected place.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.220
An unexpected place?

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.060
Yeah.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.770
You were right! I spotted some sour konbu in an unexpected place!

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.650
Sour konbu?

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.030
Dowsing? What's that?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.580
I looked it up on my Aikatsu Mobile, 
and it seems this helps you find things.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:46.080
Huh... too bad it's so drab.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.500
Now that you mention it...

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.910
Should we decorate it?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:52.670
While we're at it, why not make it a full-fledged fashion accessory?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.050
I'm getting excited for the performance.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.170
Me too!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:03.680
But to be honest, while I am looking forward to it,

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.270
I'm also kind of scared.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.440
Because you're worried that you won't ever surpass her since you admire her so much?

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.030
How did you know?

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:20.240
I felt the same way for the longest time.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.910
You did?

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.870
But not anymore.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.620
She's no longer just someone I admire—

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.080
Found one!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.330
Really?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.080
Where?

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.880
There was one in the flowerpot here.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.550
The clerk said she wouldn't mind if we took it.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.420
Amazing!

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.430
Your prediction was spot on!

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.300
Thanks!

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.890
Girls!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.890
The rain stopped! {as I type, a passing thunderstorm ended, leaving the sky a beautiful gold}

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.220
It did!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.730
Nice!

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.270
I think that's our signal to head out.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.150
Yeah!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.020
All right.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.400
Go, go!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.150
Okay!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:57.900
Go!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:58.440
Wait!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.990
Go!

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.870
That's strange. Just where is it?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.710
Is it really around here?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.800
I received a tip that it was in this area.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:23.470
Um... come on, where is that four-leaf?!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:23.470
Yotsuba{I'm absolutely certain you remember the last time you did this}{I know we've done it several times but I don't remember which was the last—was it mistarrow?}{that might've been the first, and it was that. I just didn't remember what you did, until now. Starcastle, right?}

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:24.890
Yes?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.430
Can I help you?

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.520
Yotsuba

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.520
Uh, no, what I'm looking for is a four-leaf...

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.480
Yes, like I said...

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.190
I am Yotsuba.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.280
What is this fuss about?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.700
Headmaster.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:49.160
This man here is an old acquaintance of mine. 
His name is Yotsuba Shun-san.{should there an honorific? you kept the -senpai for a similar line earlier this episode}{I messed up but would've caught it. the only ones I removed were when Yume was being silly}

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.540
I'm Yotsuba.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:57.080
For the record, according to his profile from his time as an idol,

00:12:57.080 --> 00:13:00.880
his talent is being able to hear the voices of four-leaf clovers, correct?

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.720
Yes. They call out to me wherever they are.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.180
Is that true?!

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.800
Um, yes...

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.390
I hate to bother you, but could we ask for a moment of your time?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.690
But I can't leave the shop unattended...

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.820
Would anybody care for a yummy donut?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.820
I can hear... I can hear them.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.450
Truly?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.490
Yes. I can hear the voices of the clovers.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.080
What direction is it coming from?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.830
I hear it... in that direction!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.330
On top of that hill, and also from over there.{I've seen plenty of four-leaf clovers in my day, and they were definitely not this rare}{I've never found a single one in the wild, and I've looked many a time}

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.090
From that meadow?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:43.460
Understood. I'll inform Yume at once.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:46.550
We'll split into groups and search!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.680
There's a four-leaf clover here?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.100
Yeah, according to Ako-chan.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.730
But where exactly?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.690
Leave that to us!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:02.940
Aikatsu. Aikatsu. Aikatsu.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.110
Dowsing?

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:09.320
Those rods are supposed to move in the direction of what you're looking for.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.460
Look!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.580
It's there!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.250
Wow!

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.760
The power of fashion is absolute!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.470
You said it!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:30.050
Everyone, we found it!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.680
On the name of M4 fans everywhere!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.230
We help each other in times of need!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.560
Now we have all four.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.730
Yes!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.400
Good job!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.980
All right, let's meet up at the venue entrance.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.570
I'm so happy for you!

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.860
Thanks!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.860
Yume!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.080
This way's a shortcut!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.880
Excuse us.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.430
Come on in!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.010
Akari-chan, Sumire-chan, and Hinaki-chan, right?

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.810
It's wonderful to meet you.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.270
Us too. It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.440
Mahiru told me you were coming.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.690
She said she was bringing along some charming friends.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.950
This is my sister, Yozora.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.950
Idol sisters? That's awesome!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:36.830
But she didn't say anything about how adorable you all are!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.410
We're glad to meet you too.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:40.710
Yeah! {...}{......}

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.880
Thank you for having us.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.040
Oh, right, senpai.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.670
We made these to commemorate your reunion.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.300
Four-leaf clovers?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.050
They really are.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:59.560
I went and found out what you wanted on the sly.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:05.690
Wasn't it difficult to collect four of them though?

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:10.240
We all looked for them together. Our new friends helped us too.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.200
Ako and Koharu did too.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.370
The two of them are over watching M4's performance.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.290
Subaru-kyun!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:20.660
Girls...

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.040
Thank you so much.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:29.340
The dedication you put into finding them is what I find really meaningful.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.170
Yes, I'm touched.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:37.600
They say that finding a four-leaf clover brings you good fortune.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:42.600
So to make you all as happy as can be...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.060
We'll make this the greatest performance!

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.940
Everyone, thank you for waiting.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:57.240
We invited the best people we could think of to close out the first day of Aikatsu Island.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:02.370
We of S4 would like to introduce them with love from the bottom of our hearts.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.120
Rola, get ready on standby.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.330
Got it.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:09.630
Everyone, it's time!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:14.130
This summer, they've reconvened for a limited time.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.010
The 25th generation of S4! {quarter century...}{there's an argument for spelling the number out but}

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.510
Come on out!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.630
Hello! Thank you!

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:23.760
Being able to return once again after an entire year is making my heart dance!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:30.730
The theme of this Aikatsu Island is: 
Let's envelop everyone in the Aikatsu ring.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.730
As such, we'd like to call up our wonderful new friends.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.820
Akari-chan.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.450
Can I put you on standby?

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.490
What?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:47.330
Our new friends have just made their way to the stage.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.910
I'll tell you who they are.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:57.090
The idols from Starlight Academy, Oozora Akari-chan, Hikami Sumire-chan, and Shinjou Hinaki-chan.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:04.800
I'm Oozora Akari from Starlight Academy.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.680
We're so grateful to have had the opportunity to witness such an amazing performance.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:12.890
I...

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:19.530
I started my Aikatsu after I was inspired by my cherished senpai. {cherished}

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.990
I looked up to her for the longest time.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:28.740
But now, she's no longer just someone I admire, but my pride and joy. {just pride?}{no}

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:33.870
She's an irreplaceable rival, and we push one another to greater heights through our Aikatsu.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.500
<i>Her rival...</i>

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:40.260
<i>Will I be able to view Hime-senpai like that one day?</i>

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:48.140
We met Yume-chan and the others, and I was filled with 
reassurance knowing I made partners with the same courage. {likely from the song that just played}

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.600
I'm sure we share the same worries and joys.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.350
And they were shining with all their might.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:02.650
Yume-chan, thanks so much for today.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:07.280
I wish you good luck in your Aikatsu.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:11.160
I should be the one saying that, Akari-chan.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:12.540
Thank you!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.550
Okay everyone, all together now!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:25.800
Let's envelop everyone in the Aikatsu...

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.430
Ring!

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.310
Ring!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.310
We'll meet again, right?

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.820
Remember the daytime stars, Yume-chan.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:44.400
Right, even if we can't see them...

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:48.820
Exactly. Even if they're far away, 
they're still continuing to shine out there.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:53.580
Think about us whenever you look up at the daytime stars.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.540
And us, too!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.000
Promise!

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.330
Next time we meet will be on the stage.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.590
Yeah! I know it'll happen.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.300
See ya! {this sucks}

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:05.260
Until next time.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:08.430
Bye-bye!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.010
See you again!

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:10.760
Take care!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.300
Bye-bye!

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:11.890
Goodbye!

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.560
Thank you!

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.810
<i>Akari-chan, Sumire-chan, Hinaki-chan,</i>

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.770
<i>One day... one day, together for sure!</i>

00:23:56.370 --> 00:24:01.080
Our senpai's Shine Stars Coords and their stage were shining so brightly!

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.960
We've gotta share our amazing Aikatsu with everyone too!

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:05.920
Yeah! Are you ready?

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:09.210
Let's envelop everyone in the Aikatsu ring!

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:12.930
Oh no, I think we're lost!

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:14.840
Is this a deserted island?!

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:18.390
You there! Could it be that you're lost?

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.480
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:21.940
Jungle Activities!

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:24.060
Become the first-star idol!
